{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RED ORACLE / CONTRACT CARD\n\nauthoritative_contract: The 19 inventoried OS/Python-invariant repository-policy assertions execute exactly once in the existing Ubuntu 3.13 default-suite process; all unmarked behavior in the seven mixed modules retains its original default selection; no new job or pytest session is added. Authority: this ticket ACs plus `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` platform-compatibility comments.\ntrigger_preconditions: The shared workflow expands to Ubuntu 3.11/3.12/3.13 plus macOS 3.13 and currently gives every cell the same default selector.\nproduction_path: Parse the real reusable workflow and drive real `pytest --collect-only -m` against the seven mixed modules.\ntest_tier: In-process workflow contract test; a source grep is insufficient because pytest marks may arrive from decorators, module pytestmark, or conftest hooks.\nobservable_postcondition: The repo_policy collection equals the exact 19-node set; it is disjoint from the non-policy selection; their union equals the original default selection; the primary cell receives the base selector; the other three cells receive `and not repo_policy`; the workflow still has exactly lint/pip-audit/test jobs and exactly two pytest sessions in the test job; integration remains `pytest -m integration`.\nnegative_control: Every unmarked case in the seven mixed modules remains in the non-policy selection.\nci_gate: `pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py -q`.\n\nFinal-form RED observed before any fix: both held-out tests failed (2 failed in 1.68s). The collection oracle found zero repo_policy nodes versus the required 19, and the routing oracle found no matrix-derived repo_policy selector in the default step. Failures are on the intended missing marker/routing postconditions, not import or fixture errors."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786815183765294001,"uuid":"448eac49-345e-4e64-b442-a6f2610bf5b4"}